      "block": {
        "type": "text",
        "label": "READING · MY CITY, THEN AND NOW",
        "html": "My name is Juliana, and I live in Florianópolis, a city <b>which</b> is on an island in the south of Brazil. I moved here ten years ago. Before that, I lived in São Paulo, a huge city <b>where</b> everything is fast, crowded and noisy.<br><br>I remember my last day in São Paulo very well. It was raining, and I was standing at a bus stop on Avenida Paulista <b>when</b> I suddenly thought: \"I need the sea.\" Two months later, I was living by the beach.<br><br>Today, I live in a quiet neighborhood <b>that</b> is near Lagoa da Conceição. My apartment is <b>between</b> a small bakery and a surf shop, and <b>opposite</b> my building there is a square <b>where</b> people play music on Saturdays. The people <b>who</b> live here are friendly and relaxed. Florianópolis is not as cheap as it was, and the traffic is terrible in the summer, but it is safe, green and very beautiful.<br><br>Right now, I am sitting on my balcony and I am writing this text. A man <b>who</b> sells coconuts is walking down my street, and some children are playing on the sidewalk. I usually work from home, so I go to the beach almost every day after lunch. I miss some things about São Paulo, like the museums and the food, but I don't miss the traffic!"
      }
    },
